  "extras": [],
  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "Does Garrus’s Silver (Chilling Howl) slow an enemy moving into radius from outside?",
      "answer": "No. Movement restrictions are checked at the beginning of movement, so a hero within Garrus’s radius is affected, but a hero moving into the radius will complete their full movement value.",
      "source": "goa2-faq"
    },
    {
      "question": "Can Garrus’s Alt Reds (Blunt Force) move away from the attacked hero to another?",
      "answer": "If your attack against an opposing hero does not defeat them, they will still be adjacent to you. There are several valid options for movement:\n• You could move to a different space adjacent to the hero you attacked\n• You may move and end the movement adjacent to a different enemy hero.\n• You may move and end the movement adjacent multiple enemy heroes (you can still only choose one of them as your target)\nIf you cannot end your movement next to an enemey hero, you cannot move at all after the attack.",
      "source": "goa2-faq"
    },
    {
      "question": "What are Obstacles?",
      "answer": "Obstacles are basically anything on the map: Units (Heroes and Minions), terrain shown on the map, tokens, and any other miniatures. There can only be one Obstacle on each space, and Obstacles generally can’t move through each other.\nIf an ability does allow Obstacles to pass through each other (“you can move through Obstacles”, ignore Obstacles”, “Heroes may move through a space with a tree token”), they still may not end movement on such a space.\nAny space with an Obstacle is considered occupied and not empty.",
      "source": "goa2-faq (common)"
    }
  ],
  "lore": "Garrus was the reigning champion of the Arena until his defeat at the hands of a stranger, who tricked him into losing his temper. He roams the land, seeking to regain his title and his honor. They say that his shield can deflect a point-blank ballista shot. No one has ever dared to check if it's true.",
